      | TopSecret Message Writer v1.0 Release by )/ideo /\/asty |
      `---------------------------------------------------------'

What is It?.
 TopSecret Mail Reader/Writer/Replyer is a neat utility that will allow
you to read and write true private mail to any user.

How To Install?.
 Simple copy all Supplied 3.x icons to the commands directory and copy
the supplied doors to the doors directory.

Icons: TopRead.info  < this is the icon for the reader
       TopWrite.info < this is a SPARE icon for the writer
       E.info        < this is to replace the standard E command

Writing Mail:
As you can see i have replaced the standard E command this is because
TopSecret can be used as a doorway to the normal mail routines within
AmiExpress, so EALL ALL and wildcard expansion is still possible. When
in use there will be no visable difference between TopSecret & the
normal method. This helps as users are very silly people and are very
easy to confuse.

Reading Mail:
 This works much better as a MCI command added to any autoshow text
file on logon, Remember you CAN have multiple MCI commands in any MCI
text file. This too looks and works in much the same way as the normal
read command, with a few differences.

Download Mail:
instead of Delete, the D command has bee made into a Download command
as All Private mail will be deleted on exit, also saves your msg base
being cluttered up with old mail.

 If the sysop selects this option then a Stored msg file will be
created for reading later, this allows the sysop to keep the more
important messages. I will be writing a Sysop read option into the Read
rexx, but u will have to wait for the next version for that.

Quit:
Quit is disabled as this type of mail is suppose to be force read.

Backwards:
- = Go back one message.
Normally the - is used to go in reverse but in this to go all the way
back u will have to repeat the process.

Example MCI
-------CUT------------
~CC_Wall ~CC_TopRead 
-------CUT----------^-
                    +-Leave a Space after the command

Note Commands can be stacked on the same line always remember to leve a
trailing space after any MCI command EVEN the LAST MCI command will
still require a Space or a Newline.

The above example would first do the Wall door then it would do the
TopRead door.

Now install it and let your users decide if they like it or not...

As with all my doors/utils i refuse to add AUTO SHOW BBS plugging on my
BBS i WILL NOT use doors/ utils that auto plug another bbs, and i hope
